@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+# Broadcom research consulted
+
+Accessed 2026-08-15.
+
+- [KB 392993: Minimum number of ESXi hosts required on vSAN clusters for deployment of VCF Management Domain](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/392993/minimum-number-of-esxi-hosts-required-on.html) — established the four-host minimum for a single-availability-zone vSAN management domain.
+- [KB 421094: Clarification on vSAN fault-domain failures to tolerate](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/421094/clarification-on-vsan-fault-domain-failu.html) — established that RAID-5/FTT=1 needs four hosts and that a four-node single-site cluster tolerates one host fault.
+- [KB 430632: Admin UI hangs during manual upgrade to VCF Operations 9.0.2](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/430632/admin-ui-hangs-during-manual-upgrade-to.html) — informed the supported 8.18.3-to-9.0.2 path, backup/health gates, and the requirement to keep PAK signature checking enabled.
+- [KB 398777: Re-trigger VCF Automation 9.0 failed upgrade workflow](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/398777/how-to-retrigger-vcf-automation-90-faile.html) — confirmed that Automation 8.18 is imported into VCF Operations Fleet Management before its 9.0 upgrade.
+- [KB 443395: VCF Automation 9.x upgrade database-size failure](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/443395/error-lcmvmsp10002-during-upgrade-to-vcf.html) — informed the pre-upgrade Automation database-size gate.
+- [KB 422762: Login URL after upgrading Automation 8.18 to VCF Automation 9.0](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/422762/after-upgrading-aria-automation-818-to-v.html) and [KB 434594: existing deployments after Automation upgrade](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/434594/users-unable-to-view-their-existing-depl.html) — informed abandonment of the legacy CSP URL and the mixed-case owner remediation gate.
+- [KB 402314: Aria Operations for Logs 8.18.x to VCF Operations for Logs 9.0.x](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/402314) — established greenfield parallel deployment, integration recreation, and the supported 90-day log transfer boundary.
+- [KB 402647: Windows agent availability in VCF Operations for Logs](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/402647) — confirmed continued 8.18 Windows-agent compatibility and its manual trust requirement.
+- [KB 422643: End of General Support for VMware Aria Operations 8.18](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/422643/end-of-general-support-for-vmware-aria-o.html) — established the Operations 8.18 End of General Support date of 2027-10-11.
+- [KB 318130: Automation versions and lifecycle](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/318130/build-numbers-and-versions-for-vmware-ar.html) — confirmed Automation 8.18.1 build 24282368 and its 2027-10-11 End of General Support date.
+- [KB 325701: Build numbers and versions of VMware Aria Operations for Logs](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/325701) — confirmed the inventoried Logs 8.18.3 build 24515748.
+- [KB 381187: Product Lifecycle matrix for Aria Suite](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/381187/product-lifecycle-matrix-for-aria-suite.html) and the [Broadcom Product Lifecycle Matrix](https://support.broadcom.com/group/ecx/productlifecycle) — provided the lookup method and lifecycle entry used for the Logs 8.18 support boundary, reconciled to the pinned date of 2027-10-11.
